Package: com.qingc12.pullovermf
Name: PullOverMF
Version: 0.1.6
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: MultiFloat personal fork of PullOver X (GPL-3.0). Floating multitask window / split view for iOS 14+ (roothide / arm64e). 0.1.6: ring picker interaction rework - the dial is no longer pinned to the screen centre. It is now summoned by the edge SWIPE only (the tap-to-summon shortcut is removed, a plain tap on the edge no longer opens the dial), it FOLLOWS your finger as it comes out, then locks in the centre of the LOWER half of the screen. Once locked, slide your finger over an icon to highlight it and LIFT your finger: the dial closes and the highlighted app opens in the float; lifting with nothing highlighted just closes the dial. New options: mfRingParkRatioY (0.72), mfRingLatchTolerance (72), mfRingSettleDelay (0.18), mfRingSummonThreshold (18). 0.1.5: ring picker geometry fix - the dial centre is now inset from the screen edge (screenWidth - radius - mfRingEdgeMargin) so the WHOLE circle is visible inside the screen instead of being cut in half; icons are arranged around the full 360-degree circle starting from the top (mfRingStartAngle) and the default icon size is reduced from 56 to 44pt (mfRingIconSize). New options: mfRingEdgeMargin (12), mfRingStartAngle (-90). 0.1.4: critical link fix - 0.1.2/0.1.3 failed to load entirely because PullOverX.mm is ObjC++ and called cross-file C functions declared without extern "C" (mangled refs __Z9MFLogRawCPKc / __Z19MFRingPickerInstallv could not be resolved by dyld, so the whole dylib was rejected: no handle, no log file). All shared C interfaces are now wrapped in extern "C". 0.1.3: Stheno-style ring picker summoned by a configurable edge-gesture strip (verified working above a full-screen app), tap an icon to open that app in the float, long-press to remove it (ringApps); plus pure-C MFLogRawC() file logging to /var/mobile/PullOverMF.log.
Maintainer: QingC12
Author: PullOver X by mlgm / PullOver Pro by c1d3rDev / fork by QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 14.0)
Priority: optional
